cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the OSMF Research Tracker or any of its datasets (clinical trials,
  therapeutic agents, biomarker atlases, PAIS cohorts, chronic-disease
  interventions), please cite it as below. A versioned DOI is minted for each
  GitHub release via Zenodo; cite the DOI of the release you used.
type: dataset
title: "OSMF Research Tracker: open evidence on candidate therapeutics, biomarkers and clinical trials for post-viral and chronic conditions"
abstract: >-
  Daily-updated, open-access research tracker maintained by the Open Source
  Medicine Foundation. It compiles peer-reviewed studies (PubMed), registered
  clinical trials (ClinicalTrials.gov), therapeutic-agent evidence, biomarker
  atlases and post-acute infection syndrome (PAIS) cohort data for Long COVID,
  PACVS, ME/CFS, Lyme disease, Gulf War Illness and 50+ chronic conditions, with
  druggable gene targets and candidate repurposed compounds graded by evidence
  from DGIdb, Open Targets and ChEMBL.
